The path cells for interiors have `r: undefined, c: undefined`! Bug in `interiors` construction:
```
const interiors = [...info.keys()].map(k => {
  const [r, c] = k.split(',').map(Number);
  return { r, c, ...info.get(k) };
});
```
`info.get(k)` contains `{din, dout, path}` — no r/c, so fine. But when building cells:
```
const o = info.get(kk);
...
put({ r: o.r, c: o.c, t, ... });
```
`o` from `info` lacks r/c! The interiors objects have r/c, but `info` doesn't. We need to get r/c from the key or store them in info. Fix: in the loop, parse `kk` to get r/c:
```
const [rr,cc]=kk.split(',').map(Number);
put({r:rr,c:cc,...})
```
Also tee mask branch uses `o.r`, `o.c` undefined. Need to fix all uses of `o.r/o.c` inside the cell-building loop. Let's patch by computing `const cr = +kk.split(',')[0], cc = +...` at the top and use those. Or add r,c into `info` when building. Better:
```
info.set(key(p.r,p.c), { r:p.r, c:p.c, din..., dout..., path });
```
Then `interiors` can just be `[...info.values()]`. That's clean. Let's patch.

