      .titlemeta{margin:5px 0 1px; font-size:9px}
      .bigstart{margin:7px 0 4px; padding:8px 28px; font-size:13px}
      .chaptermap{grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:6px; margin-top:6px}
      .chapter{padding:5px 6px 6px}
      .chhead{margin-bottom:3px}
      .chhead .ce{display:none}
      .levels{grid-template-columns:repeat(6,1fr); gap:3px}
      .lv{aspect-ratio:1; font-size:9px}
      .lv .ls{font-size:5px; height:6px}
      .titlefoot{margin:4px 0; font-size:7px}
    }
    ```
    With 4 chapters side by side, each has 6 level buttons in a 6-column row; buttons ~20px wide at 640px, too small. Better: 3 columns ×2 rows inside each chapter (as desktop), with 4 chapter boxes; each box ~150px, buttons ~45px. That's the desktop `.levels` 3 columns. So just switch the chaptermap to 4 columns and keep levels 3 columns. At 640px, each chapter box ~150px, buttons 45px; good. The chapter map height: 2 rows of buttons (~45px each) + header ~20 + padding ~12 = 122px. The title content: logo 42 + subtitle 10 + line 9 + tagline 2 lines 30 + meta 15 + button 30 + map 122 + footers 20 = ~280px, fits in 360 with top padding 10. Good.
    - At 430x820 portrait, the max-height 560 query doesn't apply, so the 2-column layout with larger boxes remains, and the content may fit vertically (820 tall). Good.
    - At 640x360, both max-width 820 and max-height 560 apply; the max-height query comes after the max-width query in the CSS, so it overrides the chaptermap to 4 columns. Good.
    - The titlewrap transform from the existing max-height query is `.9`; we can keep or remove. If we set a bunch of smaller sizes, keep transform .9 maybe. But with 4 columns, it might fit. Let's replace the existing `@media (max-height:560px)` block with a more comprehensive one. The current block:
      ```
      @media (max-height:560px){
        .titlewrap{transform:scale(.9);transform-origin:top center;margin-top:-6px}
        #title .chaptermap{margin-top:4px}
      }
      ```
    Replace with the enhanced block.
